// m13 — THE SLIP, then DEEP DIVE II: Everything Looks at Everything (ch09-s05's hold + ch10).
// Window 1239.34–1457.228 s (217.888 s) on the 2159.9583 s clock. One composer, one ostinato.
// ROUND-2 RE-FIT (2026-10-13): L1013 was re-narrated ("About half runs to river: softmax, to the trade.", now
//    93.83–101.70 cue-local) and everything after "river" moved +2.13 s; every anchor below is re-read from
//    narration/timeline.json (cue-local = absolute − 1239.34). Review round 2 applied: THE CANDLE OUT is now heard:
//    M1's rising fourth (E→A) and its held suspension sound in the clear gap between L1027 and L1030 (177.97–181.01)
//    at about -20 LUFS momentary in the master, the suspension arriving on the cut to the candle (180.41); the fall
//    A→G# lands in the clear after "two years" (186.66). MASKING: the cup, the "water's edge" bloom, the eight-heads
//    glow and the ledger cadence had slid under L1013/L1014/L1019/L1025 on the new clock; they are back in the gaps,
//    and the 300 Hz–3 kHz layers under those lines are thinned.
// Key: the slip motif in D (A→D over A-E, solo celesta), then A minor (the scribe) → A MAJOR on "at once"
// (the dominant: everything looks at everything) → the curtain's tap on C#, which steps up to D on "next"
// (the pivot into m14's D major). 90 BPM where there is a grid; each section's grid is re-anchored to its
// own picture beat. All times below are CUE-LOCAL seconds (absolute − 1239.34). Notes below this line that
// quote times are from earlier clocks (history); the code's anchors are the authority.
//
// RE-FIT (review round 1): every hit moved to the new clock through its beat/word name. Review notes applied:
//  * the score plucks of "two, nothing, four, two" sit in the micro-gaps AFTER each number, at D6 and above,
//    soft; the halving repeats them in the gap after "them"; no harp doubling under the numbers
//  * the pour arpeggio sounds A5 and above (celesta written ≥ a4) and lands on the cup AFTER "river"
//  * the string bed is high-passed at 150 Hz everywhere; ch10-s05..s07 are thinned (no low string drone,
//    no pulse under the cards, bells moved to D6+, the bass pulse halved in level)
//  * the join: m13 enters at 1221.59 (0.8 s fade-in) inside the gap 1221.29–1227.43; the slip sounds alone
// VOICE PASS (2026-10-11): measured speech-to-music per line (narration stem vs this render at gainDb, pre-duck) and
//    cleared every line to >= 8 dB: the scribe's pizz step and cello softer under L1002; lunch's string chords moved
//    above the voice (A4-E5, pp); the "at once" chord voiced in the outer registers only (A1-A2 + A4-A5) and the pulse
//    entering pp, because "The Transformer" follows the word "once" by 0.9 s; the heads and the matrix voices softer
//    under L1019 / L1025, with the dive's peak moved into the clear 3.4 s after "best" (IV-V-I, the ledger's cadence);
//    the six-blocks climb soft under L1021 and blooming after it; bass and pulse trimmed under the curtain.
// CRITIC r1 (2026-10-11): the densest technical lines were masked in 1-4 kHz. The high, bright voices (celesta, music box,
//    vibraphone, harp, woodblock, attention piano) now drop 6-8 dB under every line (uv(); SPEECH below) and keep their
//    level in the breaths; under L1015 the divide-by-eight arpeggio is full only in the breaths; the jam is a 0.6 s
//    burst from "tips" that stops before "cup"; the frozen E6 lands on the line's end (1337.69); the jug figure under
//    "Four words" plays only in L1011's breaths; the worked numbers sit dry and short in L1012's micro-gaps; the cup
//    chord, the unison's high octave and the M1 strings under L1030 thinner. Median 1-4 kHz margin 2.5 → 8.7 dB.
// CLOCK RE-FIT (2026-10-12, clock 2139.54 s): the window moved bodily +17.75 s (no line inside it changed length; every
//    cue-local time below was checked against narration/timeline.json and still matches to the hundredth).
// WORD PASS (2026-10-12): margins measured per spoken word (1-4 kHz, narration vs render at gainDb): the cards' last bell
//    and the jug's first glint are gone before "Four"; the halving's last pluck is short and the pour starts in the
//    micro-gap after "Pour"; the six blocks' top 'think' notes release before "Why"; the at-once chord's tails shortened
//    before "Its title"; the at-once ostinato keeps only its downbeats under "Attention Is All You Need"; M1's high
//    strings under L1030 a little thinner.
//
//   0.00–  3.74 THE SLIP        celesta A→D landing on slipPinned 2.10, A-E fifth beneath; again softer on draught 3.30
//   3.74– 13.62 THE SCRIBE      solo cello lights M1 in A (E2→A2 on "candle" 6.24); a plucked step on twos, each quieter
//  13.62– 26.70 ATTENTION       the cello holds; piano pairs high (≥E5), the 2nd note where the light lands; F lift on "bend"
//  26.70– 41.79 LUNCH           low pizz + high celesta in conversation, cutlery ticks; M1's suspension (A over E-B) on "doubted"
//  41.79– 49.11 SILENCE         "Drop the word-by-word reader" in silence; darkBeat 45.57 is the darkest point
//  49.11– 61.58 ALL AT ONCE     every voice of A major struck together on "once"; the machine ostinato locks to downbeats
//  61.58– 78.24 THREE CARDS     bells (sounding E6 / C#6 / A5) on q / k / v; M3 forward (A C# E A → C#) after "messenger"
//  78.24–106.29 THE JUG         sparse high figure; the scores in the gaps after the numbers; a pour landing after "river";
//                               a small high pour on "messages"; IV→I on "water's edge", blooming in the gap
// 106.29–126.29 DIVIDE BY 8     the arpeggio jams on one note (slam 113.26), freezes (115.53); flows warm on "soft" 117.46
// 126.29–136.91 EIGHT HEADS     on "eight" 129.35 eight voices enter one by one (M5d in A, panned); full chord in the gap 132.84
// 136.91–150.45 CLOCKS         a shuffled figure that sums the same; three ticking layers from "clock" 144.12
// 150.45–159.58 SIX BLOCKS     talk/think figure six times, a step higher each time, over the pulse; the lane pedal
// 159.58–178.29 THE MATRIX     all eight voices in UNISON on "multiplication" 165.47; cadence on "records" 171.44; the low crowd
// 178.29–189.87 CANDLE OUT     high strings carry M1 in full: E→A lit on candleOut, A over E-B, A→G# on "two" 183.75
// 189.87–215.76 THE CURTAIN    a typesetter's tap on C#; on "next" 211.03 it steps up to D (celesta), over nothing
const DUR = 217.888, BPM = 90
const VEL = 2.45         // global velocity scale (loudness trim: about -21 LUFS integrated)
// ---- seconds-based event compiler (shared by m13-m18) ----------------------------------------
// Events are [startSec, holdSec, notes, velocity, {per-event params}] in cue-local seconds. Each lane
// is compiled to one mini-notation sequence that spans SPAN seconds, then slowed to SPAN·cps cycles,
// so every onset lands exactly where the clock needs it, independent of the tempo grid.
const CPS = BPM / 240
setcps(CPS)
const SPAN = Math.ceil(DUR) + 4
const DFLT = { pan: .5, lpf: 18000, attack: .01, release: .3 }
const r4 = (x) => (Math.round(x * 10000) / 10000).toFixed(4)
function line(evs, defs) {
  defs = defs || {}
  const sorted = evs.filter((e) => e && e[0] < DUR).sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0])
  const lanes = []
  for (const e of sorted) {
    let lane = lanes.find((l) => l.end <= e[0] + 1e-6)
    if (!lane) { lane = { end: 0, evs: [] }; lanes.push(lane) }
    lane.evs.push(e)
    lane.end = e[0] + e[1]
  }
  const keys = new Set(Object.keys(defs))
  for (const e of sorted) if (e[4]) for (const k of Object.keys(e[4])) keys.add(k)
  const seq = (lane, val) => {
    let pos = 0
    const out = []
    for (const e of lane.evs) {
      if (e[0] - pos > 1e-6) out.push('~@' + r4(e[0] - pos))
      out.push(val(e) + '@' + r4(e[1]))
      pos = e[0] + e[1]
    }
    if (SPAN - pos > 1e-6) out.push('~@' + r4(SPAN - pos))
    return mini('[' + out.join(' ') + ']')
  }
  return stack(...lanes.map((lane) => {
    let p = note(seq(lane, (e) => e[2])).velocity(seq(lane, (e) => r4(Math.min(1, e[3] * VEL))))
    for (const k of keys) p = p[k](seq(lane, (e) => (e[4] && e[4][k] != null ? e[4][k] : defs[k] != null ? defs[k] : DFLT[k] != null ? DFLT[k] : 0)))
    return p.slow(SPAN * CPS)
  }))
}
// a run of notes on a grid: from t0 (inclusive) to t1 (exclusive), one onset every `step` seconds,
// cycling through `notes`; vel may be a number or a function of (i, t); len = hold as a fraction of step
function run(t0, t1, step, notes, vel, len, params) {
  const out = []
  for (let i = 0, t = t0; t < t1 - 1e-6; i++, t = t0 + i * step) {
    const n = notes[i % notes.length]
    if (n === '~') continue
    const v = typeof vel === 'function' ? vel(i, t) : vel
    if (v <= 0) continue
    out.push([t, step * (len || 1), n, +v.toFixed(3), typeof params === 'function' ? params(i, t) : params])
  }
  return out
}
// the narrator's lines (cue-local seconds, narration/timeline.json): the high, bright voices (celesta, music box,
// vibraphone, harp, woodblock, high piano) are written around them. uv(evs, k) scales an event's velocity by k and
// shortens its release when its onset falls inside a line (or 0.12 s before one); events tagged 'x' in slot 5
// are placed hits that keep their level (they sit in micro-gaps or on a picture beat).
const SPEECH = [[5.84, 12.21], [14.22, 24.59], [27.30, 33.06], [33.61, 39.35], [43.19, 50.93], [51.53, 59.95], [62.18, 75.61], [78.84, 87.85], [88.40, 93.23], [93.83, 101.70], [102.25, 106.61], [109.01, 114.40], [114.95, 118.20], [118.80, 126.97], [130.01, 134.96], [139.63, 144.39], [145.00, 150.87], [153.18, 157.38], [162.30, 170.96], [174.36, 177.97], [181.01, 186.66], [192.59, 205.57], [206.12, 213.59]]
const speaking = (t) => SPEECH.some(([a, b]) => t >= a - .12 && t < b)
function uv(evs, k, rel) {
  return evs.map((e) => (!e || e[5] === 'x' || !speaking(e[0]) ? e
    : [e[0], e[1], e[2], +(e[3] * k).toFixed(4), Object.assign({}, e[4] || {}, { release: Math.min(rel || .7, (e[4] && e[4].release) || 9) })]))
}
const X = (e) => (e[5] = 'x', e)                    // keep this hit's level
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
const B = 60 / BPM, E = B / 2, S16 = B / 4          // beat .6667, eighth .3333, sixteenth .1667
const fade = (v0, k) => (i) => v0 * Math.pow(k, i)

// ---- anchors (cue-local seconds, from narration/timeline.json) ----
const SLIP = 2.10, DRAUGHT = 3.30, CUT = 3.74                       // slipPinned, draught, the cut into ch10
const CANDLE = 6.24                                                  // candleLit ("candle")
const ATT = 13.62, BEND = 23.92                                      // ch10-s02, bend ("attention")
const LUNCH = 26.70, DOUBT = 33.58, HOLD_END = 41.70                 // ch10-s03, "Colleagues doubted it", the reading hold
const ONCE = 49.11                                                   // allLight ("once")
const Q = 67.04, K = 69.53, V = 71.60, MSG_END = 75.61, ALLCARDS = 77.01
const JUG = 78.24, MULT_END = 86.89, ADD_END = 87.85
const N1 = 89.63, N2 = 90.44, N3 = 91.16, N4 = 91.85                // the micro-gaps after "two", "nothing", "four", "two"
// round-2 clock: L1013 now runs on past "river" (99.47) to "trade" (101.70); everything after it is +2.13 s
const THEM_END = 93.24, POUR = 93.83, RIVER = 99.47, TRADE_END = 101.72, MESSAGES = 103.19, EDGE = 106.13, EDGE_END = 106.63
const DIV = 108.41, SLAM = 115.39, FREEZE = 117.65, FREEZE_END = 118.22, SOFT = 119.59, HALVED = 126.45
const EIGHT = 131.47, GLOW = 134.99
const SHUFFLE = 139.63, CLOCK = 146.25
const TALK = 153.61
const UNISON = 167.60, IV_ = 171.03, V_ = 172.37, RECORDS = 173.57, CATCH = 174.54, FOUR_T = 176.45, LOOKING_END = 177.97
const LIT = 178.62, CUT_OUT = 180.41, L1030_ON = 181.01                // THE CANDLE OUT: lit in the clear, doubted on the cut
const OUT_ = 181.32, ORDER_END = 183.73, TWO = 185.88, LINE_END = 186.66
const CURTAIN = 191.99, NEXT = 213.16, NEXT_END = 213.64
const HALVED_END = 127.02                                            // the clear after "so we halved" (L1017 ends 126.97)
const SH = 2.13                                                      // the round-2 shift, for grid literals after "river"
// ROUND-2 VOICE PASS (render 2): 1-4 kHz trims under L1002 (scribe), L1009 (the at-once chord), L1012 (the numbers),
//    L1016 (the jam), L1017 (the soft pour) and L1025 (the unison's high voices), each 2-3 dB.
// section grids carried over from the earlier clock, each re-anchored on its own picture beat
const A1 = ONCE - 41.90       // ALL AT ONCE, on "once"
const HD = EIGHT - 122.15     // EIGHT HEADS, on "eight"
const BLK = TALK - 138.40     // SIX BLOCKS, on "talk"
const MAT = UNISON - 152.39   // THE MATRIX, on "multiplication"

// ═══ CELLO (solo; the scribe, the lift, the doubt, the honest card) ═══════════════════════════════════════
$: line([
  [CUT, 2.0, 'a2', .16, { attack: .6, release: .8 }],             // the scribe's A enters at the cut, under the slip's fifth
  [CANDLE - .38, .38, 'e2', .19, { attack: .08, release: .6 }],    // M1 lit: rising fourth E→A on "candle"
  [CANDLE, 6.0, 'a2', .13, { attack: .15, release: 1.6 }],
  [ATT - .3, 4.4, 'a2', .11, { attack: .6, release: 1.2 }],        // the cello holds under "attention" (re-struck: the bow swell sits in gaps)
  [ATT + 4.2, 5.8, 'a2', .10, { attack: .8, release: 1.2 }],
  [BEND, 3.0, 'f2', .22, { attack: .5, release: 1.8 }],            // the lift on "bend"
  [DOUBT, 8.1, 'e2', .11, { attack: .5, release: .9 }],            // the doubt's floor (E under the held A)
  [LIT - .3, .3, 'e3', .13, { attack: .06, release: .3 }],          // the candle's fourth, doubled low (in the clear)
  [LIT, CUT_OUT - LIT + .3, 'a3', .13, { attack: .1, release: .4 }],
  [LINE_END + 1.4, 4.0, 'e2', .13, { attack: 1.2, release: 1.6 }],  // the honest card: one sustained note
], { attack: .3, release: 1.5 }).s('gm_cello').lpf(900).hpf(40).room(.35).rsize(3).orbit(1)

// ═══ CONTRABASS (the floor) ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
$: line([
  [ONCE, 5.2, 'a1', .10, { attack: .05, release: 1 }],
  [A1 + 47.23, 2.6, 'f#1', .12], [A1 + 49.90, 2.6, 'd2', .12], [A1 + 52.57, 1.8, 'e2', .15],
  [RIVER, 2.4, 'a1', .09, { attack: .1, release: .8 }],            // the cup fills (on "river": the cups settle)
  [EDGE + .15, .35, 'd2', .14], [EDGE_END, 1.9, 'a1', .19, { release: 1.2 }],
  [GLOW, 3.9, 'a1', .22, { attack: .2, release: 1.4 }],            // the hall glows
  [BLK + 142.40, 4.0, 'a1', .20, { attack: 1.2, release: 1 }],   // the highway lane pedal
  [UNISON, 3.2, 'a1', .11, { attack: .02, release: 1 }],           // unison
  [IV_, 1.3, 'd2', .21], [V_, 1.2, 'e2', .19], [RECORDS, .8, 'a1', .16, { release: 1.2 }],
  [CATCH - .1, 3.6, '[a1,bb1]', .10, { attack: .6, release: .8 }], // the crowd
  [LIT, CUT_OUT - LIT, 'a1', .13, { attack: .25, release: .5 }],    // THE CANDLE OUT: lit (A) ...
  [CUT_OUT, LINE_END - CUT_OUT, 'e2', .10, { attack: .3, release: .6 }],   // ... doubted (E under the held A) ...
  [LINE_END + .19, 2.2, 'e2', .12, { attack: .1, release: 1.4 }],  // ... gone (E major: A falls to G#)
  [CURTAIN + .5, 5.6, 'a1', .12, { attack: 1.5 }], [CURTAIN + 6.6, 4.4, 'f#1', .11, { attack: 1 }],
  [CURTAIN + 11.4, 5.2, 'd2', .11, { attack: 1 }], [CURTAIN + 16.9, 3.3, 'e2', .11, { attack: .8, release: .6 }],
], { attack: .3, release: 1.2 }).s('gm_contrabass').lpf(380).hpf(40).room(.3).rsize(3).orbit(1)

// ═══ PIZZ: the scribe's step on twos (each a touch quieter), lunch's low talk, the jug's pulse, the six blocks' "talk" ═══
const LUNCH_PAT = ['a2', '~', 'e3', 'c3', '~', 'e3', 'a2', '~', 'g2', '~', 'd3', 'b2', '~', 'g2', 'c3', '~']
$: line([
  ...run(CANDLE, 19.6, 2 * B, ['a2', 'e3', 'c3', 'e3'], fade(.15, .9), .5),
  // LUNCH: the low half of the conversation (8ths, below 300 Hz)
  ...run(LUNCH + .16, DOUBT - .3, E, LUNCH_PAT, (i, t) => (t < 30.4 ? .15 : .12), .6),
  // THE JUG: a soft bass pulse in halves (thinned: review asked for room under ch10-s06)
  ...run(JUG + .6, RIVER - .1, 2 * B, ['a2', 'e2'], .10, .6),
  // DIVIDE BY EIGHT: quarters under the arpeggio; drop out on the slam; back on "soft"
  ...run(DIV + .3, SLAM - .1, B, ['a2', 'e2', 'a2', 'c#3'], .10, .6),
  ...run(SOFT, HALVED - .2, B, ['a2', 'e2', 'a2', 'c#3'], .10, .6),
  // SIX BLOCKS: "talk" = two plucks a third apart, a step higher each time (A B C# D E F#)
  ...[['a2', 'c#3'], ['b2', 'd3'], ['c#3', 'e3'], ['d3', 'f#3'], ['e3', 'g#3'], ['f#3', 'a3']].flatMap(([x, y], r) => [
    [BLK + 138.40 + r * 2 * B, E * .8, x, [.13, .14, .15, .24, .27, .30][r]], [BLK + 138.40 + r * 2 * B + E, E * .8, y, [.13, .14, .15, .24, .27, .30][r]]]),
], { release: .5 }).s('gm_pizzicato_strings').lpf(1400).room(.4).rsize(3).orbit(4)

// ═══ PIANO: attention pairs (high), the "at once" chord, the eight-heads floor, the cadence ═══════════════
$: line([
  ...uv([...[['e5', 'a5'], ['c6', 'b5'], ['a5', 'e6'], ['d6', 'c6'], ['e6', 'a5'], ['b5', 'e6']].flatMap(([x, y], i) => [
    [ATT + 4.29 + i, .3, x, .12], [ATT + 4.29 + i + .33, .6, y, .15]]),
  ], .5),
  X([24.62, .3, 'f6', .16]), X([24.95, 1.4, 'e6', .19]),                     // the lift: F colour, in the breath after "attention" (round 2)
  [ONCE, 1.6, '[a1,a2,a4,e5,a5]', .04, { release: .8 }],                 // EVERY VOICE, AT ONCE (outer registers: 'The Transformer' follows at once)
  [GLOW, 1.4, '[a1,a2]', .24, { release: 1.6 }],
  [UNISON, 1.4, '[a1,a2]', .06, { release: 1.6 }],                              // unison (the high A is left to the bells)
  [RECORDS, 1.0, '[a1,a2,e3,a3,c#4]', .115, { release: .9 }],                  // the ledger's cadence
], { release: 1.4 }).s('piano').lpf(3200).room(.5).rsize(4).orbit(7)

// ═══ STRINGS (gm_string_ensemble_1): soft harmony (hpf 150, lpf), swells only in the gaps ═════════════════
